[2026-03-15T00:31:18.318Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017gevMa22kzhMthyuksGoXE","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. According to the documentation, \"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\"\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe system uses two main types of references:\n- **Points**: Specific execution moments when JS statements run or significant events occur\n- **Elements**: DOM element references independent of particular points\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened and when:\n- Error identification (UncaughtException, ReactException)\n- Timeline tools (ConsoleMessages, NetworkRequest, ReactRenders)\n- Source tools (ListSources, ReadSource, SearchSources)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** understand why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking (GetStack, ControlDependency)\n- Detail examination (DescribePoint, InspectElement, Logpoint, Evaluate)\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation recommends: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\" before using exploratory tools to identify relevant events, then explanatory tools to understand causation. The Logpoint tool is particularly useful for tracking expression values across execution points."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7da53361-7b7a-4448-be86-193d39a038b9","uuid":"8f31a477-c693-4453-8dcd-15373922fa83","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. According to the documentation, \"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\"\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe system uses two main types of references:\n- **Points**: Specific execution moments when JS statements run or significant events occur\n- **Elements**: DOM element references independent of particular points\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened and when:\n- Error identification (UncaughtException, ReactException)\n- Timeline tools (ConsoleMessages, NetworkRequest, ReactRenders)\n- Source tools (ListSources, ReadSource, SearchSources)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** understand why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking (GetStack, ControlDependency)\n- Detail examination (DescribePoint, InspectElement, Logpoint, Evaluate)\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation recommends: \"Frame your task in the form of a question that you need to answer\" before using exploratory tools to identify relevant events, then explanatory tools to understand causation. The Logpoint tool is particularly useful for tracking expression values across execution points.","durationMs":2668,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T00:31:18.326Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WnywQ8Q17LFjzbzvcYhDVv","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\n**Replay CLI** is a command-line tool that lets you \"record your application to gather performance data and debug issues.\"\n\n## Quick Start\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\nSet up authentication by creating an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and saving it to the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** – Launch Replay Browser and start recording a session\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** – Upload recordings to the cloud\n- **`replayio list`** – View all local recordings\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** – Delete recordings\n- **`replayio login/logout`** – Manage account authentication\n- **`replayio update`** – Update the Replay Browser\n\n## Common Workflow\n\nRecord a session, then upload it:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\nFor debugging with Claude, install the Replay MCP server using the provided configuration with your `REPLAY_API_KEY`.\n\n**Need help?** Run `replayio help` or add `-h` to any command for details."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7da53361-7b7a-4448-be86-193d39a038b9","uuid":"c76953d8-10d5-4921-b24f-144aa09df2fd","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\n**Replay CLI** is a command-line tool that lets you \"record your application to gather performance data and debug issues.\"\n\n## Quick Start\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\nSet up authentication by creating an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and saving it to the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** – Launch Replay Browser and start recording a session\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** – Upload recordings to the cloud\n- **`replayio list`** – View all local recordings\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** – Delete recordings\n- **`replayio login/logout`** – Manage account authentication\n- **`replayio update`** – Update the Replay Browser\n\n## Common Workflow\n\nRecord a session, then upload it:\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\nFor debugging with Claude, install the Replay MCP server using the provided configuration with your `REPLAY_API_KEY`.\n\n**Need help?** Run `replayio help` or add `-h` to any command for details.","durationMs":3535,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
